we reported earlier that Starbucks will  close its stores and corporate offices  on May 29th for a company-wide racial  bias training the announcement comes in  response to public protests and calls to  boycott Starbucks protesters are upset  about the arrest of two black men at a  Philadelphia store last week Gail is at  another Starbucks in Philadelphia  Gail good morning again thank you very  much John joining me now to discuss the  incident and how the company is handling  it is Starbucks executive chairman  that's Howard Schultz it is an interview  that you will see only on CBS this  morning and Howard we really appreciate  you taking the time to join us this  morning thank you listen we have all  heard the phrase driving while black  shopping while black and now Howard  there's a hashtag that says Starbucks  while black you see and you hear that  and you think what well I'm embarrassed  ashamed I think what occurred was  reprehensible at every single level I  think I take it very personally as  everyone in our company does and we're  committed to making it right the  announcement we made yesterday about  closing our stores 8,000 stores closed  to do significant training with our  people it's just the beginning of what  we will do to transform the way we do  business and educate our people on  unconscious cost you millions of dollars  to it'll cost it will cost millions of  dollars but I have always viewed this  and things like this as not an expense  but an investment in our people in our  company and we're better than this and I  think people expect us to be at a higher  level than many other companies and I  understand that  you know I've heard the phrase racial  bias training what exactly does that  mean people are saying to me Gail this  is just a big PR stunt this is an  overreaction  what does Howard and his company really  expect to accomplish in a training  session in an afternoon we've had two  company-wide meetings I held one in  Seattle three days ago since this  happened yes I held one yesterday here  in Philadelphia and I think the truth of  the matter is that every one of us has a  different life experience and that  different life experience  unfortunately produces a level of bias  or unconscious bias about what we feel  as people and I think we have an  opportunity with the help of sherrilyn  Ifill from the n-double a-c-p and Bryan  Stevenson and Heather McGee people who  have been in this space for a long time  to help guide us supply it's even said  of the equal justice in Asia and I want  to I want to say something that I think  is very important this is not going to  be a one-day event where we're gonna do  something and leave we're gonna sick  stay with this it's going to be  significant it's going to endure and  we're gonna transform the way we do  business I also think it's an  opportunity for healing  yesterday I I spent time with the white  manager who did make the 9-1-1 call  and it still with the company no she has  left the company I think there's a  unique opportunity for her and the two  gentlemen to sit down and potentially  have some kind of reconciliation do you  see that happening I do I think it's  gonna be possible I think she's  interested in doing it and I think kevin  has spent time with the two young men  and I think we Kevin Johnson the  Starbucks CEO yes  so perhaps something good can come out  of this and by that I mean this has  highlighted for us that we have more  work to do as a company and and I think  you know race is a very difficult  subject to discuss we learned that three  years ago you tried with the race  together race together campaign and it  did not go well no we did it didn't and  I think one of the reasons is that many  people in America are not prepared to  talk about risk I understand that but  this is a systemic problem in the  country that's not to say what happened  at Starbucks is not an issue it is an  issue and it's an issue that we will  address we will fix we take it  personally and I can promise you that I  am deeply deeply committed to  comprehensive training for our people I  would like to know more about the  conversation with the manager yesterday  what did you say what did she say how is  she feeling why did she make that call  well yeah I think for her she is  suffering herself and in her own way I  think she recognizes that perhaps that  call should not have been made  I don't think she intended when she made  the call for the police to arrive and  arrest the two young men  what did she then was gonna happen I  think she probably thought that the  police were going to talk to the men  about what they were doing and why they  were there and I think you have to say  and looking at the tape that she  demonstrated her own level of  unconscious bias and in looking at the  table ask yourself whether or not that  in fact was racial profiling yeah if is  there any doubt in your mind that the  call would not have been made had there  been two white men and you know white  customers in the store was saying look  I've been sitting here no one has said  anything to me the two black men by the  way in their 20s were there to meet a  realtor that discuss a business deal you  know there's no doubt in my mind that  the reason that they were called was  because they were african-american and I  think I'm I'm embarrassed by that I'm  ashamed of that that's not who Starbucks  is that's not who we have been and  that's not who we're going to be does  she no think she made the wrong decision  the manager I think she regrets to call  e-911 yes what if anything does a  company plan to do for the two black men  I know Kevin Johnson the CEO is met with  them have you all had any discussions  about what if anything Starbucks should  do could do for the young men I think  think about how they handle the two at  Howard I think it's actually they not  many people have recognized the fact  that this could have turned into  something much much worse that they  acted in a very passive way and thank  God for that  they were very calm and cooperative yes  yes so what we have tried to do with the  two young men and Kevin has met with  them has asked them what can Starbucks  given our resources and the capabilities  we have they have an interest in real  estate what can we do to help advise  them and support their own business and  endeavours and I think what will come  out of this is that given the resources  that we do have that we will provide  them with the foundation of learning and  provide them with an opportunity to be  part of our company either directly or  indirectly as a result of this situation  right now I have more questions yet  we're on live TV we're out of time can  you stick around and I can continue the  conversation will run the interview at 8  o'clock course I know you have another  meeting at 8 o'clock yeah for now right  now we'll send it back to you all in the  studio Thank You Gail a really good  interview and a lot of new information  there that we learned this morning about  steps that Starbucks is going to take  and about a possible meeting between  that manager and those two men thank you  so much Gail we'll look for to the rest  of that conversation
 

